THIRD-PARTY COMPONENTS

MEGATRON operates alongside separately-licensed open-source components which it does
NOT redistribute. These are installed from their upstream distribution packages at
deployment time and run as independent processes communicating over network
interfaces:

  - OpenSIPS ......... GPLv2
  - rtpengine ........ GPLv3
  - FreeSWITCH ....... MPL 2.0
  - PostgreSQL ....... PostgreSQL License
  - Redis / Valkey ... BSD-3-Clause / BSD-3-Clause
  - ClickHouse ....... Apache-2.0
  - Homer / heplify .. AGPLv3 (deployed independently; not linked or redistributed)

MEGATRON contains no source code derived from any of the above. No custom OpenSIPS,
Kamailio, or rtpengine modules are authored as part of this project, and no GPL- or
AGPL-licensed library is linked into any MEGATRON binary. This boundary is enforced
by an automated license-scan gate in CI.

See docs/ARCHITECTURE.md §3 for the full rationale and the rules this imposes on
contributors.

NOTE: This notice describes the project's engineering posture. It is not legal advice
and has not yet been reviewed by counsel. A formal review is required before first
customer distribution — see docs/ARCHITECTURE.md §9.
